<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian bank UBK shares sink 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Slovenian bank UBK shares sink 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank UBK led the day's decliners in Ljubljana on Tuesday, tumbling 10 percent on what traders said was a technical correction after recent rapid and giddy gains.</p>
<p>Since May 29, when UBK announced it would link up with Slovenia's second largest bank SKB, the bank has jumped over 43 percent on expectations of an improvement in its liquidity.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, UBK fell 10 percent or 890 tolars to 8,010 tolars on volume of 40 shares.</p>
<p>-- Novica Mihajlovic, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
